---Starts a move task for pObject.
---**Omitting Speed walks.** No default is applied on the Lua side and the doc
---calls WALK "normal", so a two-argument call is a walking call. That is the
---usual reason a worker loses half a day on the road -- not an explicit WALK,
---just a missing third argument. Of 429 movement calls under Scripts/Measures,
---118 approach legs run, 50 walk explicitly and 79 omit the speed.
---Work measures (`type = 5` in Measures.dbt) should run the approach; movement
---inside the work loop is usually deliberate and should be left alone.
---@param pObject Alias The object to move (cl_Sim/cl_Cart/...) (movingsimobject)
---@param pTarget Alias the destination to move to (eg. cl_Building/cl_Position/cl_Cart) (corenode)
---@param Speed? number moving speed (GL_MOVESPEED_SNEAK / GL_MOVESPEED_WALK / GL_MOVESPEED_RUN )
---@param Range? number The object will stop at a distance of Range before reaching the target
---@param bScheduled? boolean notifies the task tabout the measure for later progression
---@return boolean # successfully accepted move order (this does not mean that he has reached the target!)
function f_MoveTo(pObject, pTarget, Speed, Range, bScheduled) end

---Starts a move task for pObject and proceeds with the script
---See f_MoveTo: omitting Speed walks.
---@param pObject Alias The object to move (cl_Sim/cl_Cart/...) (movingsimobject)
---@param pTarget Alias the destination to move to (eg. cl_Building/cl_Position/cl_Cart) (corenode)
---@param Speed? number moving speed (GL_MOVESPEED_SNEAK / GL_MOVESPEED_WALK / GL_MOVESPEED_RUN )
---@param Range? number The object will stop at a distance of Range bevor reaching the target
---@param bScheduled? boolean notifies the task tabout the measure for later progression
---@return boolean # success
function f_MoveToNoWait(pObject, pTarget, Speed, Range, bScheduled) end

