---Directly starts a measure. Only measure's with max. two parameters can be started this way
---Dispatch is gated by DB/MeasureToObjects.dbt before any Lua runs: columns
---selectionmode, targetfilter, objectfilter, object, mouseicon, targets,
---targetflag. The filter columns are Filter.dbt ids, where **0 is `None`** -- a
---row asking for `MEASUREINIT_SELECTION` with 0 in the selection slot gives the
---player nothing valid to click, so the measure never starts and `Run()` is never
---entered. `ms_003_Walk` is the reference for a ground click: filter 1,
---`TargetFilterWalk`, accepting a Position, Sim, Cart or Building.
---Rows 90, 110, 140, 150 and 190 have **no vanilla counterpart**, so a `~` in one
---of their cells inherits nothing at all.
---@param pThisObject Alias the object that is the this object of the new measure (guildobject)
---@param pDestination Alias the destination of the measure (corenode)
---@param Measure any The measure to start. int = measure database ID / string = name of measure (Number or String)
---@param force? boolean true: force the measure to start (dont look at priorities) false: use priorities (default)
---@return string # "ok" = success / else error
function MeasureRun(pThisObject, pDestination, Measure, force) end

---forbids the measure to restart, which means the measur will cleanup instead of restart
